Modifications relative to upstream clefru/ocrmypdf-paddleocr:

  1. OCR engine replaced: PaddleOCR -> RapidOCR (PP-OCRv6)
     The engine is now rapidocr.RapidOCR driven by ONNX Runtime instead of
     paddleocr/paddlex/paddlepaddle. On CPU the two paths run the same onnx
     models, so accuracy is unchanged, but the dependency chain shrinks from
     paddlepaddle+paddlex+modelscope (with insecure and unfree packages on
     nixpkgs) to rapidocr+onnxruntime.

  2. PaddleOCR-VL support removed
     --paddle-engine vl, the PaddleOCRVL pipeline and its block/spotting hOCR
     path are gone; only the classic PP-OCRv6 det+rec+cls pipeline remains.

  3. Language set reduced to Chinese (simplified) and English
     LANGUAGE_MAP is chi_sim -> ch, eng -> en. Unsupported codes warn and fall
     back to ch. (PP-OCRv6 det/rec is one multilingual model, so both entries
     load identical weights.)

  4. Word-box handling simplified
     Upstream fetched text_word/text_word_region from PaddleOCR and re-merged
     sub-tokens and unioned their boxes. RapidOCR's return_word_box=True already
     yields (word, score, quad) per line in original-image coordinates, so the
     token merging, the doc_preprocessor_res-based scale_x/scale_y correction
     and the line regrouping helper are all removed. A proportional fallback is
     kept for lines without native word boxes.

  5. hOCR generation split into a pure function
     _hocr_document(result, width, height, hocr_lang, creator_tag) does no I/O and
     takes no RapidOCR types, so the hOCR writer is unit tested without models.

  6. Options renamed and pruned
     --paddle-engine / --paddle-inference-engine / --paddle-no-mkldnn are gone
     (onnxruntime is the backend, oneDNN does not exist here).
     --paddle-det-limit-{type,side-len} -> --rapid-det-limit-{type,side-len},
     --paddle-{det,rec,cls}-model-dir -> --rapid-{det,rec,cls}-model-path
     (RapidOCR takes model files, not directories), --paddle-use-gpu ->
     --rapid-use-gpu, --paddle-show-log -> --rapid-show-log, plus the new
     --rapid-model-type {tiny,small,medium}.

  7. Model instances are cached per process
     Upstream built the pipeline inside generate_hocr(), i.e. once per page.
     _get_rapid_ocr() delegates to an lru_cache'd builder keyed on the settings
     that change what gets loaded, so each worker loads the model once.

  8. __init__.py no longer depends on setuptools_scm; the version is read from
     package metadata. The distribution is now ocrmypdf-rapidocr (module
     ocrmypdf_rapidocr, entry point ocrmypdf_rapidocr_plugin) and
     pyproject.toml/Nix expressions were rewritten for the RapidOCR dependency
     set.

Everything else - the OCRmyPDF plugin API surface, the hOCR document structure
(ocr_page / ocr_carea / ocr_par / ocr_line / ocrx_word), polygon-to-bbox
averaging and the hOCR -> PDF path through HocrTransform - is unchanged upstream
code.

Upstream itself credits OCRmyPDF and PaddleOCR; the engine is now RapidOCR
(https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOCR, Apache-2.0) which in turn derives from
PaddleOCR's PP-OCR models.
